{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1324265-maori-creatures-in-the-world-of-darkness","id":1324265,"title":"Maori Creatures In the World of Darkness.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-13T14:07:16-07:00","id":1324265,"title":"Maori Creatures In the World of Darkness.","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://theculturetrip.com/pacific/new-zealand/articles/the-11-most-magical-creatures-in-maori-folklore/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://theculturetrip.com/pacific/new-zealand/articles/the-11-most-magical-creatures-in-maori-folklore/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://theculturetrip.com/pacific/new-zealand/articles/the-11-most-magical-creatures-in-maori-folklore/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://theculturetrip.com/pacific/new-zealand/articles/the-11-most-magical-creatures-in-maori-folklore/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What would they be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T14:31:34-07:00","id":1324271,"title":"","content":"You do the same thing that's done for any other group of folklore creatures. Some will be Bygones. Some will be Fae. Some will be monsters. Some will be fomori. Some will be spirits. Divide them according to what makes sense for you and the particular game and chronicle you'd run. Since the same creature could plausibly be slotted into multiple of the categories above, do whatever fits best for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T16:43:28-07:00","id":1324302,"title":"","content":"What would you make them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T16:58:18-07:00","id":1324305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1324265-maori-creatures-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1324302#post1324302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you make them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having read the list they seem pretty self explanatory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T00:32:52-07:00","id":1324904,"title":"","content":"What I'd make them depends on the needs of the game that I'm running. If it is Werewolf or some other Changing Breed, I'd be more inclined to make them spirits, fomori, or monsters (but the more obvious ones being fae, I'd keep fae). If I was running Mage, I'd be more willing to make them Bygones or Umbrood. If Changeling, many would be some sort of fae.<br /> <br /> There isn't any right answer. It's what you need them to be for the games you are in. You can even have &quot;one&quot; type of creature actually be a mix of spirits, monsters, and other things because human folklore can easily mix up different creatures as being the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}